   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Downing Site range on Downing Street (Sedgwick Building block): purple-red brick with Ancaster stone dressings, stone bands and pilaster strips. p0 = west end. Ground floor: two wide round-arched multi-pane windows with red-brick voussoirs (the arcade continues west onto the set-back wall :5), a pedimented stone doorcase with carved cartouche and paired columns at ~9.5 m, then narrower arched windows with a carved elephant relief panel between the first two; tall stone-mullioned transomed windows on the first floor, smaller windows in the top storey under a stone parapet. Positions located by intersecting the Mapillary camera headings with the wall line."
  },
